cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "A delta^2-L^3 Sensitivity Law for Finite-Window Weil Positivity, with a Function-Field Control of the Connes-van Suijlekom Pipeline"
abstract: >-
  A quantitative sensitivity analysis of the finite-window Weil quadratic form used in the
  Connes-van Suijlekom and Connes-Consani-Moscovici programs, calibrated against curves over
  finite fields, where the window form is the Hallouin-Perret Frobenius Gram matrix and the
  Riemann hypothesis is Weil's theorem. Proves a delta^2 sensitivity law with an L^3
  coefficient in both settings, and runs the full minimiser pipeline on deliberately planted
  off-circle spectra. Contains no proof or advance of the Riemann hypothesis for zeta.
